ECHO(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    echo - print arguments

SYNOPSIS
    echo [-n] [-e|-E] [argument...]

DESCRIPTION
    The shell builtin prints arguments separated by spaces and a newline.
    -n omits the newline, -e interprets backslash escapes and -E disables
    them. Escapes include \n, \t, \r, \b, \a, \e, \\, \0NNN and \c
    (stop output). The standalone /bin/echo is intended for plain output;
    use the shell builtin for these options.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
